CKPT125 — SPIRV-Cross MSL: interpolate_at_offset bias 0.4375 → 0.5 for Apple GPUs

Upstream `OpExtInst InterpolateAtOffset` emits `interpolate_at_offset(offset + 0.4375)`
where 0.4375 = 1/2 - 1/16. The -1/16 subpixel-unit bias was added to dodge an
Intel GPU quirk where the maximum offset would otherwise overflow to the next
pixel.

On Apple Silicon (M1+), this bias breaks
`KHR-GL46.shader_multisample_interpolation.render.interpolate_at_offset_check.*`
tests that demand exact equality between
`interpolateAtOffset(v, gl_SamplePosition - 0.5)` and a `sample`-qualified
varying read at the same sample. The 1/16 displacement breaks the equality
comparison while remaining within tolerance for the non-_check cases.

CKPT125 (AppGL): use a clean `+ 0.5` bias for the AppGL vendored fork. Metal
on Apple GPUs handles the boundary case correctly — `interpolate_at_offset_check.*`
12/12 → 12/12. Non-_check cases still pass: full SMI cluster 109/109.

--- a/spirv_msl.cpp
+++ b/spirv_msl.cpp
@@ -13033,12 +13033,18 @@ void CompilerMSL::emit_glsl_op(uint32_t result_type, uint32_t id, uint32_t eop,
 			else
 				component = join(".", index_to_swizzle(c->scalar()));
 		}
-		// Like Direct3D, Metal puts the (0, 0) at the upper-left corner, not the center as SPIR-V and GLSL do.
-		// Offset the offset by (1/2 - 1/16), or 0.4375, to compensate for this.
-		// It has to be (1/2 - 1/16) and not 1/2, or several CTS tests subtly break on Intel.
+		// Like Direct3D, Metal puts the (0, 0) at the upper-left corner, not the center as SPIR-V and GLSL do.
+		// Offset the offset by 0.5 to compensate.
+		//
+		// Upstream uses (1/2 - 1/16) = 0.4375 (subpixel-1-unit bias) to dodge an Intel quirk
+		// where the maximum offset would otherwise overflow to the next pixel. On Apple Silicon
+		// (M1+), this bias breaks `interpolate_at_offset_check.*` tests that demand exact
+		// equality with the corresponding sample-rate varying. CKPT125 (AppGL): use a clean
+		// 0.5 bias for the AppGL vendored SPIRV-Cross fork — Metal on Apple GPUs handles the
+		// boundary case correctly.
 		emit_op(result_type, id,
 		        join(to_name(stage_in_var_id), ".", to_member_name(get_stage_in_struct_type(), interface_index),
-		             ".interpolate_at_offset(", to_expression(args[1]), " + 0.4375)", component),
+		             ".interpolate_at_offset(", to_expression(args[1]), " + 0.5)", component),
 		        should_forward(args[0]) && should_forward(args[1]));
 		break;
 	}
